import csv,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];ch={}
first={x['box']:x['reading'] for x in csv.DictReader((R/'second/149_scan014_first.tsv').open(),delimiter='\t')}
def c(k,e,final=None):
 ch[k]={'personally_inspected':True,'selection':'first' if final is None else 'custom','evidence':e,'changed':'no' if final is None else 'yes'}
 if final is not None:ch[k]['final']=final
c('b02','The small low mark after barred Q has a closed oval interior, unlike the open descending comma at the far right. Retain subscript zero. The two Gamma forms, equality, doubled Qs, slash, heading underline and comma agree; mathbb braces are syntax.')
c('b05','The rotated image shows the question mark above à vérifier. Both readings preserve the same marks and words; the extra TeX line break changes only the representation of the marginal layout.')
c('b07','The repeated centralizer letter has a rounded upper turn and long lower bowl, like a cursive Z. The crop does not decide whether the alphabet should be called ordinary or script. Retain Z|mathcal Z, with ordinary Z first. All words, Gamma-Q and comma agree; mathbb braces are syntax.')
c('b08','The initial letter is the same rounded Z form as b07 and retains its alphabet doubt. The shaft has a definite rightward head. Both quotient Gammas, the Q subscript, slash and prime agree. Arrow length and dollar wrappers are representation only.')
c('b09','The initial rounded letter remains Z|mathcal Z. The following est has e loop, compressed s and tall crossed t. It is live despite retracing. The second differs only by removing alphabet doubt.')
c('b10','Both readings allow exactly the same two word forms, éléments and élémts. Their shared beginning and terminal ts are visible; the connecting run does not separate the missing/condensed en. Retain the whole-word alternative convention. The crossed equality and 1 agree; ne/neq and mathbb braces are syntax.')
c('b11','The compressed word before réduit has a low initial e-like run followed by an elevated final t return, supporting est rather than two low letters se. Inside the parentheses the numeral has a distinct right upright; the left transverse entry overlaps the opening parenthesis but does not erase that 1. Retain (1,tau), its comma, and Gamma with only barred Q: no absent denominator is supplied. Mathbb braces are syntax.')
c('b12','Both centralizer letters match the curved Z family of b07–b09, preserving its alphabet doubt. Tau, the crossed membership sign, comma, donc, equality, parenthesized 1 and final point agree.')
c('b13','The left glyph has two open curved lobes and no prime, contrasting with the straight stem and three arms of the ordinary E on the right. Retain script-E/epsilon uncertainty. Epsilon/varepsilon and order of alternatives describe the same unresolved form here; the edition keeps its established epsilon command. Inclusion, complete barred-K/K index and comma agree.')
c('b15','The centralizer letter is again the rounded Z form, so its existing alphabet doubt stays. Dans, the ordinary E with its three arms, and the full barred-K/K index agree. Bar/overline is syntax.')
c('b16','The last tall stroke is t with a looped foot and a long low terminal return. That return could include a compressed e, but no independent e loop is secure. Make réduite|réduit explicit instead of deciding by agreement with image. The Gamma, accent, à, braces, numeral 1 and comma agree; the clipped upper brace tip is identified from its surviving middle and lower curves.',first['b16'].replace('réduite',r'\unsure{réduite|réduit}'))
c('b17','The rounded Z retains its alphabet uncertainty. The two-leg kernel letter matches the established lowercase pi forms and their indexed position on scans009–013; angular shape alone does not require capital Pi. The inclusion and complete barred-K/K index agree; dollars and bar spelling are syntax.')
c('b18','All three two-leg signs use the same form as the kernel in b17. Keep lowercase pi consistently; the first prime, inclusion, equality and full barred-K/K index are all visible. Dollar wrappers and bar spelling are syntax.')
c('b19','The first curved letter has a clearly detached prime and retains the script-E/epsilon alphabet doubt. The following word begins with a low s bend, not the tall ascending d and left bowl required for dans. Its u trough and extended r return support sur. The final two-leg sign is the same lowercase pi family as b17–b18, and the comma is clear. Prime placement and epsilon/varepsilon spelling are representation only.')
c('b20','The thin digits are 1 and 3, with a slanted entry to 1 and two lobes in 3. Their small scale, pale hand and extreme lower-left position identify separate foliation. Retain margin rather than the author-page wrapper.')
